WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:02.782
- So the second craziest
Trump surrogate lawyer,

00:00:02.782 --> 00:00:04.080
question mark,

00:00:04.080 --> 00:00:05.020
LinWood,

00:00:05.020 --> 00:00:07.990
who has been filing all
sorts of crazy lawsuits

00:00:07.990 --> 00:00:10.620
and ai a QAnon conspiracy peddler,

00:00:10.620 --> 00:00:11.790
has been making all kinds

00:00:11.790 --> 00:00:13.970
of crazy accusations about John Roberts,

00:00:13.970 --> 00:00:15.420
the Chief Justice of the Supreme Court.

00:00:15.420 --> 00:00:16.840
Woods says that Roberts knew

00:00:16.840 --> 00:00:18.910
that Scalia was going
to die before he did.

00:00:18.910 --> 00:00:20.596
That Roberts arranged

00:00:20.596 --> 00:00:22.440
an illegal adoption of two young children

00:00:22.440 --> 00:00:23.706
from Wales through Jeffrey Epstein.

00:00:23.706 --> 00:00:26.470
And then Woods questions whether
John Roberts skipped a day

00:00:26.470 --> 00:00:27.640
of defamation class,

00:00:27.640 --> 00:00:29.330
implying that the allegations are true.

00:00:29.330 --> 00:00:30.398
Therefore not subject to defamation.

00:00:30.398 --> 00:00:31.560
So the question is,

00:00:31.560 --> 00:00:33.196
are these allegations
subject to defamation?

00:00:33.196 --> 00:00:35.182
And the answer is almost certainly yes.

00:00:35.182 --> 00:00:38.010
Chief Justice Roberts is
not going to sue Lin Woods.

00:00:38.010 --> 00:00:39.578
He probably doesn't know who Lin Woods is.

00:00:39.578 --> 00:00:40.680
But these are the kinds

00:00:40.680 --> 00:00:42.224
of verifiable provable facts

00:00:42.224 --> 00:00:44.860
that could definitely give
rise to a defamation claim.

00:00:44.860 --> 00:00:47.220
So if you found this interesting or sad,

00:00:47.220 --> 00:00:48.570
check out my other Eagle briefs

00:00:48.570 --> 00:00:50.220
where I talk about the legal news.

00:00:50.220 --> 00:00:51.353
I'll see you in court.

